==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology===
First appeared in the Russian magazine {{w|Ogoniok}} in 1928. {{w|Mikhail Koltsov}}, the magazine's founder, applied the term to a selection of puzzles in the magazine. He had named the feature after a fellow employee who prepared the feature, {{l|ru|'''[[Виктор]]''' [[Микул'''ин''']]}}. Later, people began to associate his puzzle with the Latin term {{m|la|victor||winner}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|виктори́на}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Cinemantique-викторина.wav}}

===Noun===
